{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon","id":836805,"title":"How to make a dragon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-24T19:13:55-08:00","id":836805,"title":"How to make a dragon?","content":"Me and my players are eager to try how the changeling play test will look like in play, but i had a question about one of my player. He has the concept of playing a dragon of legends so he picked draconic and gargantuan kith for his character. The problem is he wants to breathe fire and the closest contract he can buy right now is control the elements but it doesn't fit as much as he would like. Is there a way I could help him in a war or another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11309-krishtan","name":"krishtan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:45:55-08:00","id":836816,"title":"","content":"You could have him trade out one of his other kith blessings for fire breath, (Maybe the fighting style dots from gargantuan?) or you could homebrew a contract, either a seeming variant to elements or something totally new. <br /> <br /> Based on existing material, breathing fire would most likely be a dex+athletics roll, with Wyrd added to either the dice pool or as a weapon modifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:52:44-08:00","id":836817,"title":"","content":"I think the Chrysalis contract would work perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T20:03:20-08:00","id":836824,"title":"","content":"So his problem is that he wants to play Beast: the Primordial, essentially.<br /> <br /> Hunt around for suitable Goblin Vow purviews or possibly change out one kith for Ifrit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T22:36:24-08:00","id":836865,"title":"","content":"If he wants to be a fire breathing dragon and doesn't want to change out a kith for ifrit, the contract riddle-kith could essentially give him the ifrit kith as a permanent third kith (or for however long he is willing to reduce his clarity maximum to 9 for), though he'd have to carry a source of flames with him in order to 'breathe' fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T22:45:01-08:00","id":836867,"title":"","content":"Just use the Elemental Contracts, just don't have him start with it yet. You can't have everything at start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T01:59:22-08:00","id":836928,"title":"","content":"I'd use Riddle Kith to add Windwing, honestly. What good is a dragon that can't fly? Control Elements can probably do what you want it to. It's pretty flexible. Plus the Wyrd almost certainly knows what a dragon is so it's not too hard to justify tweaking the cosmetics of the contract to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T04:14:33-08:00","id":836954,"title":"","content":"Well, you can do 3 things here to acomplish that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Modyfing Kiths</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to the option of players and Storytellers working together to create entirely new kiths, they can also modify existing ones.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Get the Dual-Kith Merit (rename it to Greater Kith, or something, the effect of the merit is the same). Get Draconic and Windwing, now let's change some of the kith's blessings:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2. Modify a little here:<br /> Draconic (Or Greater Draconic Kith part I)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">His thick scales transform the first Wyrd points of lethal damage he takes in a turn into bashing damage and he can do lethal damage with his unarmed attacks. <s>He can spend a point of Glamour to add Wyrd to all Intimidation rolls for the scene.</s> He can spend a point of Glamour to unleash a breath of fire, he rolls Dexterity + Athletics and add half his Wyrd(rounded down) to the damage modifier.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3. Modify a little there:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Windwing(Or Greater Draconic Kith part II)</span><br /> The windwing can fly at twice his Speed for as many turns as he has dots in Stamina, but must spend a turn without a movement action before he can fly again. <s>Spend a Glamour to increase the duration of his flight to a minute per Wyrd.</s> During flight, he can use his Defense against Firearms. <s>The windwing can land and perch on anything capable of holding a small child, regardless of his real weight.</s> The windwing can spend a point of glamour and a instant action to grow to titanic proportions, add half her wyrd(rounded up) to her size for the scene.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 02-25-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T06:06:31-08:00","id":836992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>krishtan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon#post836805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He has the concept of playing a dragon of legends so he picked draconic and gargantuan kith for his character. The problem is he wants to breathe fire and the closest contract he can buy right now is control the elements but it doesn't fit as much as he would like. Is there a way I could help him in a war or another?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, remember that we don't have all the Contracts. Even Ifrit with its pyrokinesis can't create fire from nothing, which is what you'd want.<br /> <br /> What I suggest is that you adapt Contracts of Eternal Summer 5 to the new system. Shouldn't be too hard to convert, and while its not fire, super heated breath of super sunlight that burns people is actually a pretty awesome replacement.<br /> <br /> Another option is to create a new Seeming variation for Cloak of the Elements. Lets say Beast for the sake of simplicity. &quot;You can shoot the cloak at a target and not just damage through touch; make a standard ranged attack, with an weapon bonus equal to your Wyrd.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT - also, I like the Chrysalis option someone mentioned. The actual mechanics aren't hard to write.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon?p=836824#post836824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So his problem is that he wants to play Beast: the Primordial, essentially.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dragons were in CtL long before Beast came out. I've played a dragon in 1e CtL twice now to good effect. I mean, otherwise, if someone said they wanted to play a Cherion Group hunter, would you be saying &quot;Oh, he just wants to play Deviant!&quot; or &quot;that's supposed to be a Lost Boy!&quot; Immortal undead from Egypt - a mummy or is that a vampire? After all, we do have information on vamps in Ancient Egypt from the books. Or how about a very old Sin-Eater, which was hinted as a tier 3 krewe? Or an Osiran prommie?<br /> <br /> Concepts do overlap between games. &quot;Dragon&quot; is hardly unique to Beast the Primordial. Calling it a &quot;problem&quot; and that she really wants to play another game is rather unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-25-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T06:47:56-08:00","id":837001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon?p=836928#post836928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd use Riddle Kith to add Windwing, honestly. What good is a dragon that can't fly? Control Elements can probably do what you want it to. It's pretty flexible. Plus the Wyrd almost certainly knows what a dragon is so it's not too hard to justify tweaking the cosmetics of the contract to fit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> HEY, there are land and sea dragons too, pal! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Darn fliers getting all the attention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I think the best option is to reduce / modify his dragony powers. Otherwise he's going to have a very quick drop into madness if he's flying around, breathing fire and slicing people with his claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-25-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T06:57:17-08:00","id":837002,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think the problem is that while full-blown dragons are totally a Changeling thing, they're not really a <i>changeling</i> thing. It's the sort of shit the Gentry would get up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:07:12-08:00","id":837006,"title":"","content":"I wrote a fire-breathing kith for 1e for one of my players with the exact same wish. I've modified it for 2e; it might help if your player wants a more area-of-effect attack, rather than a single hit or the Pyrokinesis merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Doomspitter</b><br /> <i>You break into my house, steal my tokens, and expect mercy? Oh no, little worm, I'm going to make you <b>burn</b>. </i><br /> Doomspitters embodied the monsters that deal death from a distance: chimeras that spew fire, serpents that spit acid, banshees that shout pain, and, of course, dragons. Many were set to guard a castle or treasure, some were set in coliseum battles, and others were taken to fill the fairy-tale of the hero slaying the beast.<br /> <i>Beast</i>: A lion's head, goat's body, and snake's tail, panting flames<br /> <i>Darkling</i>: Wrinkled, haggard face, wrapped in a dark cloak, whose screams shatter glass<br /> <i>Ogre</i>: A hulking lizard-man, with lashing tail and jaws dripping fire<br /> <b>Blessing</b>: Doomspitters are immune to any damage, Conditions, or Tilts caused by the element they spit, such as fire, acid, or sound (chosen at character creation). Wyrd times per scene, they can spend a point of Glamour to spit that element. The Doomspitter picks a center point within 20 feet; the effect targets everyone except the Doomspitter in a close range of that point. The Doomspitter rolls Dexterity + Athletics; everyone else in the area contests with Dexterity + Athletics. Dramatic Failure: The attack goes wild, causing 2 lethal damage to the Doomspitter, or to an area of the GM's choice. Failure: The shot fizzles out in your throat, or a target dodges out of the way. No damage. Success: The target doesn't dodge, or doesn't dodge well enough: targets take 1 lethal damage for every success the Doomspitter gets above them. Exceptional Success: As a success, and the target takes an appropriate Condition (such as Sick, On Fire, Pain-Wracked, or Chilled).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:52:19-08:00","id":837028,"title":"","content":"In dreams he can literally become a fire breathing dragon, with an enviromental fire breath attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T08:20:14-08:00","id":837037,"title":"","content":"That's true, but he could also become a giant chainsaw-juggling clown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T11:08:53-08:00","id":837103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon?p=836992#post836992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragons were in CtL long before Beast came out. I've played a dragon in 1e CtL twice now to good effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A dragon out of legend,&quot; complete with fire-breathing and being a huge armored monstrosity, meanwhile, is fairly solidly in Fae territory if you're expecting to pull that kind of thing off outside of Arcadia within the normal aesthetics of changelings and Contracts as available to a starting character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, otherwise, if someone said they wanted to play a Cherion Group hunter, would you be saying &quot;Oh, he just wants to play Deviant!&quot; or &quot;that's supposed to be a Lost Boy!&quot; Immortal undead from Egypt - a mummy or is that a vampire? After all, we do have information on vamps in Ancient Egypt from the books. Or how about a very old Sin-Eater, which was hinted as a tier 3 krewe? Or an Osiran prommie? </div> </div> </div>Comparing the very specific &quot;my player has already picked two kiths that resonate with Atavisms and is having trouble with the available fire magic not really matching a third&quot; to &quot;someone wants to play a splat from one game that could be conceptually replicated in another&quot; is extremely disingenuous and I'd appreciate if we could refrain from immediately lowering the level of discourse to ad absurdum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Calling it a &quot;problem&quot; and that she really wants to play another game is rather unfair. </div> </div> </div>OP used the word. I would not have used the word otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T11:41:12-08:00","id":837121,"title":"","content":"I have nothing useful to contribute, but the title of this thread compels me to make a joke:<br /> \u200b<br /> The more important questions is &quot;How to <i>train</i> a dragon?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T11:50:14-08:00","id":837128,"title":"","content":"To be fair, playing a beast in an otherwise-changeling game is something Beast is built to handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:39:01-08:00","id":837162,"title":"","content":"If the only problem is breathing fire, you could let him make a goblin contract to get dragonfire atavism from beast. Make the cost equitable to gaining a 3 dot contract. Hell they could get the low Satiety for when the changeling is low a clarity, even better they could pay a clarity for the Satiety expenture effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 02-25-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:04:21-08:00","id":837174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon?p=837103#post837103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A dragon out of legend,&quot; complete with fire-breathing and being a huge armored monstrosity, meanwhile, is fairly solidly in Fae territory if you're expecting to pull that kind of thing off outside of Arcadia within the normal aesthetics of changelings and Contracts as available to a starting character.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've done it in 1e. Yes, as a starting character. It wasn't exactly effective, since the amount of power behind the chosen abilities was pretty weak, but it was thematically coherant dragon themed character. <br /> <br /> So, sorry, but I'm firmly going to disagree with you on this one. I've done it. I've seen others do it. Its possible in 1e. In 2e, with its higher power level? It should be just as viable.<br /> <br /> Futhermore... who said anything about a starting character? The OP didn't. For all we know, the player in question might be willing to wait to get their ability, or use some combination of traits. We just know that they're not happy with Control Elements to mimic fire breath. That's it. Assuming anything beyond that is just that - an assumption on your part. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Comparing the very specific &quot;my player has already picked two kiths that resonate with Atavisms and is having trouble with the available fire magic not really matching a third&quot; to &quot;someone wants to play a splat from one game that could be conceptually replicated in another&quot; is extremely disingenuous and I'd appreciate if we could refrain from immediately lowering the level of discourse to ad absurdum. </div> </div> </div> What is disingenuous is suggesting that someone really wants to play a character of another game just because both games happen to let you play different takes on dragons. There's no reason to bring BtP up at all. <br /> <br /> In another thread, I said that I made up a Darkling Fireheart/Ifrit (fireheart can generate flame, ifrit can manipulate existing flame) Black Rose character. Lots of fire, darkness, and social abilities. That's kinda demonic. Does that mean I essentially want to play Demon: the Descent, or perhaps Demon the Fallen, or even Inferno? No. I don't want to play a fallen angel of any sort - I want to play a human character that went through literal and figurative hell to get back to their loved one. I like the drama of being tempted to feast on his emotions. Just a sip, even though it could hurt. Even more insidiously, being tempted to sup on emotions when lover boy gets really angry or upset, and mellow him out. <br /> <br /> Before David released all that playtest material, I was talking to my group about a vampire game that would jump up and down the ages as the vampires remembered events from times between torpor. Does that mean I want to play Mummy? No. I don't want an Egypt theme, I don't want to hunt down Relics or ancient mysteries. I want to keep the blood drinking, the saint-sinner feel of Vampire, the dancing and socio-politics through the eternal night.<br /> <br /> Playing a canine-themed Gangrel, Orphean of Proteus, Cuprum Refined prommie, Beast 'ling, or Begotten, it doesn't mean that the player wants to play Werewolf: the Forsaken. Even if the player does take a few powers that are similar to Uratha shifting and hunting. And its disingenuous to suggest it is. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OP used the word. I would not have used the word otherwise. </div> </div> </div> The opening post used the word in context of &quot;there's no Contract that really mimics fire breath.&quot; You then flipped it around to make it about what the player wants being the problem. Having a kith called <i>Draconic</i> suggests that playing a dragon in Changeling is part of the core game. If there's a problem, its not on part of the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T09:18:22-08:00","id":837615,"title":"","content":"Maybe dual-kith into Ifrit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:09:06-08:00","id":837835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon?p=837615#post837615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe dual-kith into Ifrit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally suggested that in my first post, but it seems MCN is more concerned with intimating that <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default58fd.html?g=posts&amp;m=1710663#post1710663\" target=\"_blank\">I have somehow transformed into the complete opposite of the person I was two years and change ago</a> and that my joking that someone whose salient character details are &quot;is large, armored, and intimidating, and would like to breathe fire but is at a point where 'the closest contract he can buy right now' is Control the Elements&quot; as part of a concept of &quot;a dragon of legend&quot; (where kiths are drawn from what you <i>were</i> in Arcadia and inform what you may become as you grow more like the Fae) is looking for something that Beast: the Primordial is literally built for is comparable to saying that running a Vampire game whose primary narrative widget <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61284/Ancient-Mysteries\" target=\"_blank\">had a book partially dedicated to it three years before Mummy was even announced</a> is indicative of wanting to instead play the much more particular game of Mummy: the Curse.<br /> <br /> The takeaway here is that it would be really great if the OP could actually get back here and respond to some of the suggestions that have been made so that an incidental comment does not wind up continuing to be ballooned into absurdity for reasons that I find difficult to fathom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:15:03-08:00","id":838706,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your help. There was a lot of good suggestions but I think I will use Horodrigo's suggestion for now since it's quite easy to try. When I said dragon of legends i didn't think about a crazy powerful dragon but more about the aesthetic, sorry if it confused people. I know he is a starting character and even thought he would not be able to necessarily to get everything at start, it is something he would like to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11309-krishtan","name":"krishtan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:59:15-08:00","id":838836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>krishtan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon?p=838706#post838706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks everyone for your help. There was a lot of good suggestions but I think I will use Horodrigo's suggestion for now since it's quite easy to try. When I said dragon of legends i didn't think about a crazy powerful dragon but more about the aesthetic, sorry if it confused people. I know he is a starting character and even thought he would not be able to necessarily to get everything at start, it is something he would like to achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad I could help.<br /> I'm mixing some other kiths and have obtained a fair amount of cool concepts, I'll share them later on the topic of &quot;Multi-Kith Merit 2e&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T22:19:10-08:00","id":841727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>krishtan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836805-how-to-make-a-dragon#post836805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to make a dragon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When a mommy dragon and a daddy dragon love each other very much....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}